            <ArticleTitle>[Three cases of spontaneous mediastinal emphysema].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>477-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report 3 cases of spontaneous mediastinal emphysema. All patients were young males, and had predisposing episodes for development of spontaneous mediastinal emphysema; sports in 2, loud voice in 1. The each chief complaint was dyspnea, throat pain, and epigastric pain. Two patients were admitted, but 1 rejected admission despite sufficient informed consent. All patients became asymptomatic with mediastinal air reabsorption within a week. We should recognize spontaneous mediastinal emphysema as one cause of chest, back, neck and epigastric pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
